    "https://www.concordia.ca/hr/jobs/pay-equity.html": {
      "title": "Pay equity",
      "description": "Pay equity | Human Resources - Concordia University Our site uses cookies. They allow us to remember your preferences, better serve you and give us information on how you interact with our site. To find out more about our use of cookies, please read our Cookie Notice . Accept all Reject all Manage preferences × A cookie is a very small text document stored on your computer or other device (and maintained by your browser) when you visit a website. It often includes a randomized unique identifier so that a website can “recognize” this cookie again on your next visit. Cookies allow the functioning of websites, improve browsing, or provide certain information to website owners, particularly in terms of audience measurement. Cookies do not cause any damage to your device, but they facilitate, for example, finding preferences, pre-filling certain fields or adapting the content of the services on the visited site. Such data allow us to improve the ergonomics of our site and our services according to your interests. To find out more about our use of cookies, please read our Cookie Notice . Accept all User Consent Legitimate Interest Essential cookies These cookies are essential for you to browse the website and use its features, such as accessing secure areas of the site. Cassie Banner SyrenisGuid_ This cookie stores the data subject's visit unique id for the consent. Concordia Hub Description is currently not available Delete Cookie Delete Cookie Performance cookies These cookies collect information about how you use our website, like which pages you visited and which links you clicked on. None of this information can be used to identify you. It is all aggregated and, therefore, anonymized. Their sole purpose is to improve website functions. Cassie Banner Performance_Cookie Performance_Cookie Google Analytics _ga_ custom ID used to identify users Marketing cookies These cookies track your online activity to help us deliver more relevant advertising or to limit how many times you see an ad. These cookies can share that information with third parties. Cassie Banner Marketing_Cookie Marketing_Cookie Functional cookies These cookies allow our website to remember choices you have made in the past, like what language you prefer, what your user name and password are and other similar preferences. Cassie Banner Functional_Cookie Functional_Cookie Save preferences Open Cookie Settings Skip to main content Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Hub Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) All academic resources IT services Library Safety & prevention Exchanges & partnerships Printing Wi-Fi access Concordia app Apply Visit Give fr Sign in For students Student Hub For faculty & staff Carrefour Human Resources Concordia Directories Search Search Close Careers Working at Concordia Current opportunities Employment equity Salary scales Pay equity Pension & benefits Pension & benefits overview Health plan Dental plan Pension plan Group RSP Life insurance plans Accident insurance plan Pensioners' Corner Employee Assistance Program Labour agreements Training & development About HR Meet HR Contact HR Policies & forms News & notices Glossary Apply Visit Give Useful links Maps Safety & prevention Wi-Fi access Printing IT support Library Contact us Concordia app Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) Exchanges & partnerships All academic resources fr Open search form Concordia University Human Resources Careers Pay equity Pay equity The main objective of a pay equity plan is to: Determine if discriminatory treatment exists in the compensation of female-dominated job classes when compared to male-dominated job classes of similar value Rectify their compensation if such practices should exist. Pay equity process To learn more about the pay equity process, you can also refer to the following websites: Commission de l’équité salariale Pay Equity Act Contact Please contact us by email: payequity@concordia.ca Pay equity Pay Equity Programs FAQ Back to top © Concordia University Human Resources Careers Pension & benefits Labour agreements Training & development About HR Contact us Concordia employee? Log in to Carrefour Contact us 514-848-2424, ext. 3666 Fax: 514-848-2844 hr-reception@concordia.ca Get in touch with HR Office hours Monday to Friday: 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. Visit us Room FB-1130 (11th floor) 1250 Guy St. Montreal, QC  H3H 2S7 Faubourg Building (FB) Mailing address Concordia University Attn. Human Resources 1455 De Maisonneuve Blvd. W. Montreal, QC  H3G 1M8 CANADA Territorial acknowledgement Concordia University is located on unceded Indigenous lands. The Kanien’kehá:ka Nation is recognized as the custodians of Tiohtià:ke/Montreal. Central 514-848-2424 | Emergency 514-848-3717 Safety & prevention | Accessibility | Privacy | Terms | Cookie settings | Contact us | Site feedback © Concordia University.  Montreal, QC, Canada"
    },
    "https://career17.sapsf.com/career?company=universitc": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Career Opportunities JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities  Search for Opportunities Keywords: Show help, How does keyword search work?\n Enter a list of words, and we’ll search for them in the job title, or you can choose to search for them also within the job description.\n Tips:\n \n We will find results for any words listed in the search\n Results beginning with words searched will also be returned. Ex: A search for “Manage” will return “manage, manager, management” etc.\n To find an exact phrase, surround your search phrase with double quotes (” “). Ex: “senior manager”, or check ‘Exact match’.\n \n \n Advanced search:\n \n Use AND, OR, NOT, and () to combine search terms. Ex: Sales AND engineer finds only jobs that have both terms. \n Sales OR engineer finds all jobs that have either. \n (Sales AND Engineer) NOT Manager finds jobs that contain both “Sales” and “Engineer” but not “Manager”.\n Use question mark (?) for an unknown letter. Ex: Thomps?n finds Thompson, Thompsen, Thompsan, etc.\n Use tilde (~) to find similar spellings. Ex: roam~ finds roam, roams, room, road, roads, etc.\n Do not use advanced search options if you have checked ‘Exact match’. Keyword search options Exact Match in job title in job title or description Posting Language:  Select one or more options for Posting Language multiselect combobox with checkbox options.No value selected Division:  Select one or more options for Division multiselect combobox with checkbox options.No value selected Department:  Select one or more options for Department multiselect combobox with checkbox options.No value selected Posted within the last: days Campus:  Select one or more options for Campus multiselect combobox with checkbox options. No value selected Full-time / Part-time:  Select one or more options for Full-time / Part-time multiselect combobox with checkbox options. No value selected Updating... No jobs matched. Try widening your search. 11 Jobs match the selections Emphasized Search Jobs Clear * Name of Saved Search/Alert: Field is required. * Email me: Field is required. - Select - Daily Weekly Every Two Weeks Never Field is required. Send email only when new jobs are available Send email only when new jobs are available Welcome to Concordia Careers! Would you like to pursue a career at Concordia University? Come join a team that addresses society’s big challenges, supports your personal and professional growth, and makes a real impact to build a more sustainable world. Learn more about the benefits of working at Concordia . What positions are posted on Concordia Careers? Within Concordia Careers, you will find non-academic staff positions. Faculty and other academic and research positions can be found on the current job opportunities page. If you are a current Concordia employee, visit the Job opportunities page in My HR (UNITY) to apply. Join our talent community Step 1. Create your profile: Create an account by clicking on \"Sign In\" at the top of the screen and fill out the required information. Once logged in, upload your resume and complete your profile with the required information. Save your profile. Step 2. Use \"Search Jobs\" to find opportunities: To see all positions that are currently open, simply click on the blue “Search Jobs” button. To filter jobs, type in a key word or use one of the search boxes. Don't see the right opportunity currently available? Use your profile to register for alerts. Step 3. Apply for available opportunities: Did you find a position that interests you? You can apply in just a few minutes using your Concordia Careers profile. Click on Apply, add a cover letter and, if required, answer any additional questions. Check your email and the Job Management section on your profile to monitor the status of your application. Concordia is committed to employment equity In line with its commitment to employment equity , Concordia collects applicant equity information on a voluntary basis during the recruitment process. Need help? Consult the How to apply page for additional support in your application process. Accommodations are available for applicants throughout the recruitment process. If you require accommodations for interviews or other meetings, or for any further information or assistance, please contact Human Resources at hr-employment@concordia.ca ."
    },
    "https://www.concordia.ca/hr/jobs/openings/external-candidates.html": {
      "title": "Instructions for external candidates",
      "description": "Instructions for external candidates | Human Resources - Concordia University Our site uses cookies. They allow us to remember your preferences, better serve you and give us information on how you interact with our site. To find out more about our use of cookies, please read our Cookie Notice . Accept all Reject all Manage preferences × A cookie is a very small text document stored on your computer or other device (and maintained by your browser) when you visit a website. It often includes a randomized unique identifier so that a website can “recognize” this cookie again on your next visit. Cookies allow the functioning of websites, improve browsing, or provide certain information to website owners, particularly in terms of audience measurement. Cookies do not cause any damage to your device, but they facilitate, for example, finding preferences, pre-filling certain fields or adapting the content of the services on the visited site. Such data allow us to improve the ergonomics of our site and our services according to your interests. To find out more about our use of cookies, please read our Cookie Notice . Accept all User Consent Legitimate Interest Essential cookies These cookies are essential for you to browse the website and use its features, such as accessing secure areas of the site. Cassie Banner SyrenisGuid_ This cookie stores the data subject's visit unique id for the consent. Concordia Hub Description is currently not available Delete Cookie Delete Cookie Performance cookies These cookies collect information about how you use our website, like which pages you visited and which links you clicked on. None of this information can be used to identify you. It is all aggregated and, therefore, anonymized. Their sole purpose is to improve website functions. Cassie Banner Performance_Cookie Performance_Cookie Google Analytics _ga_ custom ID used to identify users Marketing cookies These cookies track your online activity to help us deliver more relevant advertising or to limit how many times you see an ad. These cookies can share that information with third parties. Cassie Banner Marketing_Cookie Marketing_Cookie Functional cookies These cookies allow our website to remember choices you have made in the past, like what language you prefer, what your user name and password are and other similar preferences. Cassie Banner Functional_Cookie Functional_Cookie Save preferences Open Cookie Settings Skip to main content Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Hub Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) All academic resources IT services Library Safety & prevention Exchanges & partnerships Printing Wi-Fi access Concordia app Apply Visit Give fr Sign in For students Student Hub For faculty & staff Carrefour Human Resources Concordia Directories Search Search Close Careers Working at Concordia Current opportunities Employment equity Salary scales Pay equity Pension & benefits Pension & benefits overview Health plan Dental plan Pension plan Group RSP Life insurance plans Accident insurance plan Pensioners' Corner Employee Assistance Program Labour agreements Training & development About HR Meet HR Contact HR Policies & forms News & notices Glossary Apply Visit Give Useful links Maps Safety & prevention Wi-Fi access Printing IT support Library Contact us Concordia app Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) Exchanges & partnerships All academic resources fr Open search form Concordia University Human Resources Careers Current opportunities Instructions for external candidates Instructions for external candidates How to apply for a non-academic job on the Concordia Careers website if you are not currently employed by the university. Step 1: Create your profile Create an account by clicking on \"Sign In\" at the top of the screen and fill out the required information. Once logged in, upload your resume and complete your profile with the required information. Save your profile. Learn more in this guide [PDF] Step 2: Use \"Search Jobs\" to find opportunities To see all the current open positions, simply click on the blue “Search Jobs” button. To filter jobs, type in a key word or use one of the search boxes. If no current opportunities match your interests, you can use your profile to set up personalized alerts. Consult this guide to find out how [PDF] Step 3: Apply for available opportunities The application process takes a few minutes.  Simply click \"Apply,\" include a cover letter, and, if required, answer any additional questions. Upon submission, you will receive a notification confirming that your application has been successfully received. Consult the guide for more information [PDF] Selection phase The Concordia Talent team will start reviewing the applications received once the job posting has closed. Check your email and the \"Job Management\" section on your profile to monitor the status of your application. Step 4: Pre-interview Candidates selected for an interview will receive an update on their profile along with two notifications: A request for additional information such as references, a declaration of relationship and copies of relevant diplomas. A request to select an interview slot. You will be able to select the time slot that best suits you on a first-come, first-served basis. Please note that some departments may choose to contact you directly to schedule your interview. In this case, you will receive only the first notification. Step 5: Post-interview and pre-employment assessments If additional interviews are required, you will receive new notifications to schedule the additional interviews. If you are one of the preferred candidates, the talent team will contact you to schedule any required pre-employment assessments, such as computer and language tests, scenario testing, or fitness for duty. At this stage, the Talent team will also proceed with verifying the references provided. Step 6: Letter of offer Congratulations! If you've reached this stage, you have been selected for the position you applied for. The Talent team will be in touch to discuss the offer and any additional details. Consult the guide for more information. The offer will be uploaded to your candidate profile for you to review and sign. Learn more in this guide [PDF] Need help? For any further information or assistance, please contact the Concordia Talent team at hr‑employment@concordia.ca . Go to the Concordia Careers website Back to top © Concordia University Human Resources Careers Pension & benefits Labour agreements Training & development About HR Contact us Concordia employee? Log in to Carrefour Contact us 514-848-2424, ext. 3666 Fax: 514-848-2844 hr-reception@concordia.ca Get in touch with HR Office hours Monday to Friday: 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. Visit us Room FB-1130 (11th floor) 1250 Guy St. Montreal, QC  H3H 2S7 Faubourg Building (FB) Mailing address Concordia University Attn. Human Resources 1455 De Maisonneuve Blvd. W. Montreal, QC  H3G 1M8 CANADA Territorial acknowledgement Concordia University is located on unceded Indigenous lands. The Kanien’kehá:ka Nation is recognized as the custodians of Tiohtià:ke/Montreal. Central 514-848-2424 | Emergency 514-848-3717 Safety & prevention | Accessibility | Privacy | Terms | Cookie settings | Contact us | Site feedback © Concordia University.  Montreal, QC, Canada"
    },
