nt advertising or to limit how many times you see an ad. These cookies can share that information with third parties. Cassie Banner Marketing_Cookie Marketing_Cookie Functional cookies These cookies allow our website to remember choices you have made in the past, like what language you prefer, what your user name and password are and other similar preferences. Cassie Banner Functional_Cookie Functional_Cookie Save preferences Open Cookie Settings Skip to main content Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Hub Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) All academic resources IT services Library Safety & prevention Exchanges & partnerships Printing Wi-Fi access Concordia app Apply Visit Give fr Sign in For students Student Hub For faculty & staff Carrefour Tuition & Financial Aid Concordia Directories Search Search Close Tuition & fees Tuition & fees overview Tuition & fee estimates University fees Cost of living Deadlines for payment Paying tuition Refunds Tax receipts Scholarships & funding Loans Loans overview Quebec loans & bursaries Federal & provincial loans U.S. loans Employment Find a job Work-study program Campus jobs by unit Budgeting & banking Budgeting & banking overview Budgeting Canadian bank accounts Credit cards Financial Literacy Month Financial and personal safety Apply Visit Give Useful links Maps Safety & prevention Wi-Fi access Printing IT support Library Contact us Concordia app Info for Future students Current students Alumni & friends Faculty & staff Employers Parents Media Quick links Undergraduate Welcome Guide Graduate Welcome Guide Academic dates Student Service Centre (Birks) International Students Office (ISO) Exchanges & partnerships All academic resources fr Open search form Concordia University Students Tuition & Financial Aid Employment Campus jobs by unit Campus jobs Gain valuable work experience on campus during your studies. See which areas of the university hire students and where to find job postings. Find work as a student on campus Explore paid opportunities to develop your skills and support the ongoing operations at Concordia. The Exams Office As an invigilator, administer all aspects of an exam and act as the primary contact in the exam room. See job postings The Student Success Centre Work as a study group leader, peer tutor, writing assistant, Welcome Crew mentor, First Stop assistant, FutureBound program assistant and more. See more job postings The Welcome Centre Show Concordia in its best light when you greet future students at the Welcome Centre as a campus tour guide. Jobs posted on HOJO The Access Centre for Students with Disabilities Work as a note taker, transcriber, accessibility facilitator and more. See job postings Recreation & Athletics The team often hires referees, scorekeepers, timekeepers, ticket sellers and more. See job postings Hospitality Concordia Work as a front desk clerk or join the housekeeping staff when you join the Hospitality Concordia team. Jobs posted on HOJO University Advancement Student ambassadors connect with alumni, parents, friends and students by phone to raise money and build meaningful relationships. See jobs postings. Or, join the alumni events team as a student event assistant, where your main focus will be providing onsite logistical help. Jobs posted on HOJO , Career Services job bank and Facebook . Espace Franco Work with francophone students undertaking post-secondary studies in English for the first time as an ambassadeur/ambassadrice at Espace Franco . Find job postings on Instagram CU Wellness Peer wellness ambassadors at CU Wellness empower students to cultivate well-being. Jobs announced via newsletter GradProSkills Facilitate workshops designed to help fellow grad students expand their technical, professional and academic skills. Learn more Homeroom As a student facilitator or program assistant in a Homeroom pod, you'll help new students navigate their university experience. Find job postings on Instagram Career Management Services, John Molson School of Business Join the Career Management Services team as a work-study coordinator for business students. Jobs posted on the CMS career portal More paths to employment Work-study Work up to 20 hours a week if you're in financial need. Apply now Campus Ex-L Take on a short- or long-term project through campus experiential learning. Find paid positions Work off campus Take a look at job banks for Concordia students. Browse jobs © Concordia University Tuition & financial aid Tuition & fees Scholarships & funding Loans Employment Budgeting & banking Contact us Visit us Room GM-230.00 1550 De Maisonneuve Blvd. W. Guy-De Maisonneuve Building (GM) Contact us 514-848-2424 , ext. 3507 Fax: 514-848-3508 fundingyoureducation@concordia.ca Mailing address Financial Aid and Awards Office 1455 De Maisonneuve Blvd. W. Suite GM-230 Montreal, QC  H3G 1M8 Territorial acknowledgement Concordia University is located on unceded Indigenous lands. The Kanien’kehá:ka Nation is recognized as the custodians of Tiohtià:ke/Montreal. Central 514-848-2424 | Emergency 514-848-3717 Safety & prevention | Accessibility | Privacy | Terms | Cookie settings | Contact us | Site feedback © Concordia University.  Montreal, QC, Canada"
