 available on and off campus. Find a job on campus Many areas of the university need students throughout the year on a full- and part-time basis. It's a great, flexible way to gain valuable work experience and complement your studies. Work-study program Find jobs offering up to 20 hours per week if you meet the program's financial criteria. Apply to the program Campus jobs by unit Explore job opportunities offered by units across campus. Find campus jobs Campus Ex-L Through the Campus Experiential Learning program, you'll find opportunities to work on short- or long-term projects across many departments. Learn more Explore jobs off campus Browse various job banks offering work to Concordia students off campus. Hojo job bank Concordia Student Union (CSU) Concordia Student Union's Off-Campus Housing and Job Resource Centre listings See the listings CAPS online job bank Career Advising and Professional Success Find full-time work, part-time work, summer jobs and internships in your field. Employers post over 300 positions each month for both current students and alumni. Search CAPS's online job bank External job search websites Career Advising and Professional Success Access an extensive list of job search websites both on and off campus. Search for on- and off-campus jobs Job, career and internship resources Job and internship search resources Career Advising and Professional Success Get advice on writing résumés and cover letters, improve your interview skills and find where to look for jobs and internships. Find resources Job search resources Career Advising and Professional Success Master the art of the job search, and succeed in finding the internship you want. Find resources 5 great places to start your student job hunt at Concordia Concordia news story Concordia Student Union's Off-Campus Housing and Job Resource Centre listings Read the story © Concordia University Tuition & financial aid Tuition & fees Scholarships & funding Loans Employment Budgeting & bankin